# Swift quality

Applies to all Swift code under `ios/`.

## Language & safety

- **No force unwraps (`!`), force casts (`as!`), or `try!`** outside tests. Use `guard let`, `if let`, optional chaining, and typed `throw`s.
- Model domain values with **structs and enums**, not dictionaries or stringly-typed data. IDs get dedicated types (`UserID`, `MessageID`).
- All server DTOs are `Codable` structs that mirror the Rust definitions; when one side changes, update the other in the same change set.
- Use `async/await` and structured concurrency; UI state mutations happen on `@MainActor`. No `DispatchQueue` sprinkling in new code.

## Architecture

- **MVVM**: SwiftUI views are declarative and dumb; logic lives in `ObservableObject`/`@Observable` view models; services (crypto, network, storage) are protocol-backed so they can be mocked in tests.
- Views never talk to the network or database directly.
- Crypto/key material is only touched through the dedicated crypto service (`security-crypto.mdc`); it never appears in view or view-model code.

## SwiftUI

- Build screens from the shared design-system components (`design-system.mdc`); no ad-hoc paddings, colors, or font sizes in feature views.
- Every screen supports Dynamic Type, dark mode, and VoiceOver labels on interactive elements.
- Previews (`#Preview`) are required for every new view and must render without network access.

## Before "done"

- Project builds without warnings; `xcodebuild test` passes; SwiftFormat/SwiftLint (when configured) clean (`regression-testing.mdc`).
